    <!-- 006 is included AHEAD of the shared-core bootstrap deliberately (SCRUM-91), and the
         position is load-bearing. 000 carries the same un-cascaded guarded drop of the
         `mandate` projection that all ten M-services carry, and CockroachDB refuses an
         un-cascaded drop while a view still selects from the table. MRG's man_ext_status is
         the only view that ever did; the changeset that built it is gone, but a database
         migrated by a jar built between 003 and 006 still carries the view. Retiring it here,
         before the shared core runs, is what converges that state instead of failing every
         migration. Everything else keeps its numeric order. -->
